y constants:\n\n\\( (75 + 117i) \\cdot 4 = 300 + 468i \\), and \\( \\frac{96 + 144i}{4} = 24 + 36i \\).\n\nSo, same as before: \\( (300 + 468i)e^{i\\theta} + (24 + 36i)e^{-i\\theta} \\).\n\nSo, perhaps, we can write this as \\( (300 + 468i)(e^{i\\theta} + e^{-i\\theta}) + (24 + 36i)(e^{-i\\theta} - e^{i\\theta}) \\).\n\nWait, no, that might complicate things. Alternatively, perhaps express in terms of cosines and sines.\n\nLet me write \\( e^{i\\theta} = \\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta \\) and \\( e^{-i\\theta} = \\cos\\theta - i\\sin\\theta \\).\n\nSo, substitute into the expression:\n\n\\( (300 + 468i)(\\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta) + (24 + 36i)(\\cos\\theta - i\\sin\\theta) \\).\n\nNow, let's compute each term:\n\nFirst term: \\( (300 + 468i)(\\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta) \\).\n\nMultiply out:\n\n= 300\\cos\\theta + 300i\\sin\\theta + 468i\\cos\\theta - 468i^2\\sin\\theta\n\n= 300\\cos\\theta + 300i\\sin\\theta + 468i\\cos\\theta + 468\\sin\\theta\n\n(Since \\( i^2 = -1 \\), so -468i^2 sin\u03b8 = 468 sin\u03b8 )\n\nSimilarly, second term: \\( (24 + 36i)(\\cos\\theta - i\\sin\\theta) \\).\n\nMultiply out:\n\n= 24\\cos\\theta - 24i\\sin\\theta + 36i\\cos\\theta - 36i^2\\sin\\theta\n\n= 24\\cos\\theta - 24i\\sin\\theta + 36i\\cos\\theta + 36\\sin\\theta\n\nNow, combine both terms:\n\nFirst term: 300cos\u03b8 + 468sin\u03b8 + (300i sin\u03b8 + 468i cos\u03b8)\n\nSecond term: 24cos\u03b8 + 36sin\u03b8 + ( -24i sin\u03b8 + 36i cos\u03b8 )\n\nSo, adding both together:\n\nReal parts: 300cos\u03b8 + 468sin\u03b8 + 24cos\u03b8 + 36sin\u03b8 = (300 + 24)cos\u03b8 + (468 + 36)sin\u03b8 = 324cos\u03b8 + 504sin\u03b8\n\nImaginary parts: (300 sin\u03b8 + 468 cos\u03b8)i + (-24 sin\u03b8 + 36 cos\u03b8)i = [ (300 sin\u03b8 - 24 sin\u03b8) + (468 cos\u03b8 + 36 cos\u03b8) ]i = (276 sin\u03b8 + 504 cos\u03b8)i\n\nSo, the entire expression is \\( (324\\cos\\theta + 504\\sin\\theta) + i(276\\sin\\theta + 504\\cos\\theta) \\).\n\nTherefore, the real part is \\( 324\\cos\\theta + 504\\si